agnostic Sciences To provide specialized office assistance, coordinating procedural business or service activities for a complex program area involving processing, implementing, advising on, and reporting specialized subject matter. View Details Bookmark Office Assistant I 07/22/2026 S02800 3170 - Counseling Center To perform a variety of multi-step clerical procedures required for the maintenance and support of a unit. View Details Bookmark Accounts Payable Coordinator 07/17/2026 S02791 4765 - Accounts Payable Coordinates payment documents being received by Accounts Payable, accurately assessing compliance to OU policies and other related requirements, completing the weekly payment run with payments being processed timely and accurately in conjunction with established policies and procedures. View Details Bookmark Facilities Business Coordinator 08/04/2026 S02767 4858 - Facilities Business Management To coordinate and process assigned work orders and business activities in the Facilities Business Office. View Details Bookmark Physician Assistant Program Coordinator 09/04/2026 S02826 0729 - Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences The Physician Assistant (PA) Program Coordinator provides administrative, operational, andlogistical support to the Physician Assistant Program. The Program Coordinator ensuresefficient day-to-day operations while supporting compliance with accreditation standards,university policies, and program objectives. This position requires a highly organized, proactiveindividual who excels in planning, ... View Details Bookmark Director of Academic Success 08/27/2026 S02824 0100 - School of Medicine In support of the Associate Dean for Student Affairs and Enrollment Management and Assistant Dean for Student Affairs, the Director of Academic Success provides strategic leadership and support at the Oakland University and William Beaumont University Hospital campuses for academic support/learning assistance, career advising, and program development. The Director will lead the Academic Success... View Details Bookmark Assistant Director of Advising 09/01/2026 S02825 0090 - Nursing As the School of Nursing (SON) has continued to grow, so has the number of advisers and programs. The Assistant Director of Advising will be responsible for the day-to-day operational needs for advising services. The Assistant Director will be instrumental in developing and supporting targeted initiatives aimed at enhancing nursing-specific orientations, registration, academic progress, and ove... View Details Bookmark Museum Technician 08/28/2026 S02827 3760 - Meadow Brook Estate Under the supervision of the curator, this position cleans historical interior elements, rooms, and collections at Meadow Brook Estate, ensuring a safe, clean environment for Meadow Brook Hall’s historical resources.This position will carry out routine building and collections care duties according to schedules and seasonal needs. The person will identify the need for any non-routine building m... View Details Bookmark Assistant Director 08/24/2026 S02821 2140 - Pre-College Programs Provide leadership and management for university-sponsored college access and readiness programs that expand educational opportunities and promote postsecondary success for pre-college students. Assists with the planning, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of federally, state, and university-funded pre-college initiatives while ensuring compliance with grant requirements and... View Details Bookmark Compliance Coordinator 09/04/2026 S02831 4112 - Legal Affairs/Gen Counsel/Bd Of Trustees To assist the Assistant Athletic Director for Compliance, who reports to the General Counsel, in the coordination of athletic rules and NCAA compliance for Oakland University intercollegiate athletics. All duties must be performed in a manner consistent with NCAA, conference and Oakland University rules, regulations, ordinances, policies, procedures and guidelines. View Details Bookmark Art & Practice of Medicine Course Coordinator 08/26/2026 S02822 0100 - School of Medicine Reporting directly to the Director, Clinical Skills Training and Simulation, the SP Coordinator will provide administrative support for the Clinical Skills Center (CSC), located at the Troy campus of Beaumont Hospital. The coordinator will function as an initial point of contact for the CSC. The coordinator is responsible for administrative processes in the center including scheduling, purchasi... View Details Bookmark Medical School Curriculum Coordinator 08/13/2026 S02818 0100 - School of Medicine Reports to the Curriculum Program Administrator for the Office of Medical Education. The Medical School Curriculum Coordinator will provide administrative support for curricular programs across all four years of the undergraduate medical education program of the Oakland University William Beaumont School of Medicine. View Details Bookmark Assistant General Counsel 08/13/2026 S02817 4112 - Legal Affairs/Gen Counsel/Bd Of Trustees Assist the General Counsel in providing legal services to the University on an extensive range of legal matters including without limitation general business, board governance, constitutional law, compliance, governmental immunity, intellectual property, patent, copyright, health care, labor and employment, employee benefits, tax, contracts, academic and policy issues, real estate and construct... View Details Bookmark Grants & Contracts Officer 08/13/2026 S02816 2701 - Office of Research Administration Under general supervision, administers and facilitates grant preparation, submission, and post-award management for university faculty. Advises and assists departments with process and compliance issues related to funding agency regulations and standards, and oversees adherence to university administrative, fiscal, and accounting policies and procedures related to grants and contracts. View Details Bookmark Executive Director of Treasury Management 08/07/2026 S02815 4483 - Finance & Administration Provide strategic leadership and oversight for the University’s treasury management functions, including debt administration, working capital investments, endowment investments, and related financial operations. Ensure the prudent stewardship of institutional financial resources through effective investment management, debt financing, liquidity planning, risk management, and policy development ... View Details Bookmark Video Support Technician 08/20/2026 S02814 7159 - Communications & Marketing The Video Support Technician supports the university’s strategic marketing and communications efforts through the creation of high-quality video and audio content while providing operational support for the Creative Media Team’s production facilities. Responsibilities include filming, video editing, podcast production, sound design, and supporting the production of campus events.The position co... View Details Bookmark Director of Title IX and Compliance 07/22/2026 S02807 4811 - Chief of Staff Responsible for investigating, reporting and training related to the following areas: Title IX, Equal Opportunity, and Americans with Disabilities Act and attendant duties. View Details Bookmark Communications Manager, Office of the Provost 08/07/2026 S02806 7159 - Communications & Marketing The Communications Manager serves as the primary communications resource for Academic Affairs—owning the day-to-day execution of the Provost’s communications plan while also bringing strategic judgment and independent initiative to the role.This is a standalone embedded position. The Communications Manager operates with a high degree of autonomy, managing the full scope of Academic Affairs comm... View Details Bookmark Associate Vice President and Controller 07/24/2026 S02810 4483 - Finance & Administration Provide strategic leadership and oversight for the University’s accounting services functions, which include responsibility for the University’s general ledger system, and related fund accounting practices. Lead and support directors across Central Accounting, Accounts Payable, Student Business Services, Payroll, and Purchasing. Direct the development and implementation of financial policies an... View Details Bookmark Testing Coordinator/ Disability Coordinator 07/17/2026 S02803 3210 - Disability Support Services This hybrid role supports the mission of the Disability Support Services (DSS) office by coordinating accommodated testing services (75%) and performing disability intake and accommodation assessments (25%). Reviews and processes all exam appointment requests submitted by students and communicates follow-up questions as needed. Manages faculty communications related to student exam appointments... View Details Bookmark Regional Admissions Adviser 07/17/2026 S02801 2609 - Admissions Ensure that prospective students are recruited, admitted, and oriented to the university and assist in the facilitation of recruitment, yield, and transition programs.This is a remote position based in Kalamazoo, Michigan or the surrounding area. The employee must have a home office space in Kalamazoo or the surrounding area, with reliable, high-speed internet and telephone access. A laptop, pr... View Details Bookmark Coordinator for Learning Communities 07/16/2026 S02802 3118 - Housing Residential Life The Coordinator for Learning Communities develops and coordinates residential learning initiatives that support student engagement, academic success, and community building. Through collaboration with faculty, campus partners, and Housing staff, this position creates and assesses programs and experiences that promote student learning, belonging, and retention while providing support for student... View Details Bookmark Graduate Student Services Coordinator 07/17/2026 S02798 2347 - Graduate School The Graduate Student Services Coordinator supervises and oversees the team that supports the graduate student lifecycle from application through graduation, and will have overall responsibility for the programs and students assigned to their subteam. These responsibilities include serving as a liaison among the Graduate School, students and programs; monitoring students’ progress; assist in int... View Details Bookmark Admissions Adviser 07/13/2026 S02796 2609 - Admissions Ensure that prospective students are recruited, admitted, and oriented to the university and assist in the facilitation of recruitment, yield, and transition programs. View Details Bookmark Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support 07/07/2026 S02788 2621 - Registrar The Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support in the Office of the Registrar plays a key role in advancing the university’s commitment to student success. This position designs, develops, implements, and maintains digital processes, reports, and dashboards in accordance with established best practices, ensuring data integrity and reliability. The Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems ... View Details Bookmark Manager of Electrical and Plumbing Department 07/02/2026 S02785 4300 - Facilities Management Plan, organize and supervise facility maintenance and services dealing with building electrical, plumbing, and elevator components and systems. View Details Bookmark Security Coordinator 07/08/2026 S02783 3760 - Meadow Brook Estate This position is responsible for maintaining a safe and secure environment for patrons and employees of Meadow Brook Hall by establishing and enforcing security policies and procedures and monitoring the premises and personnel. View Details Bookmark Previous 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 Next 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
