      "title": "Oakland University: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.oakland.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs Oakland University: All Jobs 2026-03-27T15:39:36-04:00 https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37301 2026-03-27T15:39:35-04:00 2026-03-27T15:39:36-04:00 Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Physical Therapy <div>The Physical Therapy Program in the Department of Human Movement Science at Oakland University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate or Full Professor position beginning August 15, 2026.<br><br></div><div>We seek a dynamic educator–scholar committed to advancing physical therapy education, clinical practice, and translational research. The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty within the School of Health Sciences and contribute to teaching in the Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) curriculum while developing a program of scholarship supported by strong clinical partnerships, research infrastructure, and mentorship opportunities.<br><br></div> 0738 - Human Movement Science https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38952 2026-09-04T15:55:07-04:00 2026-09-04T15:55:07-04:00 Graduate Student Services Coordinator <div>The Graduate Student Services Coordinator supervises and oversees the team that supports the graduate student lifecycle from application through graduation, and will have overall responsibility for the programs and students assigned to their subteam. These responsibilities include serving as a liaison among the Graduate School, students and programs; monitoring students’ progress; assist in interpreting policy and ensuring compliance; and serving as a professional resource for academic programs.</div> 2347 - Graduate School https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38540 2026-07-30T00:02:24-04:00 2026-07-30T00:02:25-04:00 University Services Mover <div>Transports furniture, office equipment, and related items within the university campus and off-campus as needed. Operates vehicles and mechanical equipment as required to facilitate loading, unloading and transport of materials, as appropriate to the area of operation. Routinely interacts with all constituents in the campus community.</div> 4858 - Facilities Business Management https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37992 2026-06-04T14:21:27-04:00 2026-06-04T14:21:27-04:00 Special Instructor in Accounting <div>The School of Business Administration at Oakland University seeks to fill a Special Instructor of Accounting position. This is a full-time position with job security track. The person who fills this position will likely teach graduate and/or undergraduate introductory financial and managerial accounting courses. Depending on her/his qualifications, the person may also teach data analytics in accounting, accounting information systems, taxation, and auditing. He/she will also work with the accounting student organizations and provide guidance on a career in accounting. The normal teaching load is seven classes per academic year. Class sizes are moderate. Summer teaching is usually available for an additional stipend. The successful candidate will provide evidence of effective teaching or training, relevant professional experience, and experience interacting with business professionals. Candidates must demonstrate effective communication skills. The ability to collaborate effectively with other faculty members, intent to engage in scholarly/professional activity, and evidence of professional accomplishments are desirable. The salary is competitive, and the fringe benefits are excellent.</div> 0460 - Accounting & Finance https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38969 2026-09-04T16:11:32-04:00 2026-09-04T16:11:33-04:00 Director of Academic Success <div>In support of the Associate Dean for Student Affairs and Enrollment Management and Assistant Dean for Student Affairs, the Director of Academic Success provides strategic leadership and support at the Oakland University and William Beaumont University Hospital campuses for academic support/learning assistance, career advising, and program development. The Director will lead the Academic Success Team, supervise the monitoring of all student progress, and manage accommodation implementation for disability support. The Director will serve as a generalist career advisor for M1-M4 students as part of the Career Advising Team. The Director will work independently to prioritize assignments and strategies to achieve the mission of the School of Medicine under the direct supervision of the Assistant Dean for Student Affairs.</div> 0100 - School of Medicine https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36359 2025-10-29T11:57:40-04:00 2025-10-29T11:57:41-04:00 Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Department of Counseling at Oakland University, Rochester, Michigan is seeking applicants for a Tenure-Track position in Counseling (Clinical Mental Health or School Counseling), as either the assistant or associate professor rank. The position is a full-time appointment with the possibility of summer teaching starting January 6, 2026. Responsibilities include teaching, research, and service activities. We will begin reviewing applications on November 3, 2025 and continue reviewing applications until the position is filled. The Department of Counseling values high-quality teaching, research, service, and is committed to social justice, diversity, equity, and inclusion. The primary responsibilities of the position include:<br><br></div><div>1. Teach courses at the masters and doctoral-levels<br><br></div><ul><li>Teach across the CACREP curriculum including clinical courses</li><li>Advise students and supervise doctoral student dissertations</li><li>Engage with curriculum planning and development<br><br></li></ul><div>2. Research and Scholarship<br><br></div><ul><li>Engage in an active and sustained research agenda</li><li>Mentor and engage in collaborative research and scholarship with students</li><li>Foster an environment of intellectual curiosity<br><br></li></ul><div>3. Service<br><br></div><ul><li>Engage in service assignments at the Department, School, and University level</li><li>Engage in community service with community partners and clinical sites</li><li>Engage in professional leadership within the counseling profession<br><br></li></ul> 1770 - Counseling https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38888 2026-08-28T11:58:43-04:00 2026-08-28T11:58:44-04:00 HR Internship Coordinator 6227 - Organizational Leadership https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38584 2026-08-05T10:04:49-04:00 2026-08-05T10:04:49-04:00 Assistant Professor of Education <div>The Department of Human Development and Child Studies (HDCS) at Oakland University invites applications for a tenure-track, benefits-eligible faculty position at the rank of <strong>Assistant Professor to begin in August 15, 2027</strong>.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will join the Special Education area and contribute primarily to the Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA) graduate program. Responsibilities include teaching graduate coursework in ABA, mentoring graduate students, maintaining an active scholarly agenda, and contributing to departmental, school, university, and professional service activities.</div><div>The standard teaching load is 3 courses in one semester and 2 courses in the other semester. Teaching responsibilities will include mentorship and supervision of graduate students enrolled in the program's Experiential Learning/Exit Project sequence and may include courses such as Experimental Analysis of Behavior, Behavior Change Procedures, and other graduate-level ABA courses consistent with the candidate's expertise and program needs.</div><div>The successful candidate will contribute to the continued growth and quality of the ABA program, including support of ABAI Recognition and future accreditation efforts. Candidates with interests that complement existing faculty expertise and who demonstrate potential for future leadership within the program are especially encouraged to apply.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications will begin <strong>September 7</strong> and continue until the position is filled.</div><div><br></div><div>For further information, please contact the Chair of the Search Committee:</div><div>Dr. Michael Kranak</div><div><a href=\"mailto:kranak@oakland.edu\"><strong>kranak@oakland.edu</strong></a></div> 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37354 2026-04-02T14:42:19-04:00 2026-04-02T14:42:20-04:00 Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy <div>The Physical Therapy Program in the Department of Human Movement Science at Oakland University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning August 15, 2026.<br><br></div><div>We seek a dynamic educator–scholar committed to advancing physical therapy education, clinical practice, and translational research. The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty within the School of Health Sciences and contribute to teaching in the Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) curriculum while developing a program of scholarship supported by strong clinical partnerships, research infrastructure, and mentorship opportunities.<br><br></div> 0738 - Human Movement Science https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38954 2026-09-04T15:56:09-04:00 2026-09-04T15:56:10-04:00 Regional Admissions Adviser <div>Ensure that prospective students are recruited, admitted, and oriented to the university and assist in the facilitation of recruitment, yield, and transition programs.<br><br><strong><em>This is a remote position based in Kalamazoo, Michigan or the surrounding area. The employee must have a home office space in Kalamazoo or the surrounding area, with reliable, high-speed internet and telephone access. A laptop, printer and basic office supplies will be provided; the employee will need to furnish other office space needs beyond these items. OU will provide a rental vehicle during peak recruitment travel periods. Mileage will be given when personal vehicle usage is necessary outside of the peak recruitment season, when a rental is not provided.</em></strong></div> 2609 - Admissions https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38049 2026-06-10T15:27:37-04:00 2026-06-10T15:27:37-04:00 Accompanist <div>The music department has a 19 hour (weekly) cap on casual staff (accompanist). Due to the influx of students in our program, our current staffing cannot meet the needs for our students are we require and additional accompanist to cover all assignments in applied music.</div> 1203 - Music, Theatre & Dance https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38976 2026-09-04T17:28:04-04:00 2026-09-04T17:28:05-04:00 Facilities Business Coordinator <div>To coordinate and process assigned work orders and business activities in the Facilities Business Office.</div> 4858 - Facilities Business Management https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36678 2025-12-19T08:39:16-05:00 2025-12-19T08:39:16-05:00 Assistant Professor <div>The Oakland University School of Nursing is seeking applications for exceptional nurse researchers and educators for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor to meet the needs of growing programs to begin August 15, 2026. Candidates must hold a current Michigan Registered Nurse license or be eligible for Michigan RN licensure.<br><br></div><div>Expertise in acute care, maternal-child/OB, pediatrics (prefer pediatric acute care NP certification), leadership, psych/mental health nursing (prefer PMH NP certification), simulation, forensic nursing, or adult-geriatric NP (primary care or acute care) is desired, but all qualified applicants will be considered.<br><br>The School of Nursing provides high-quality and accessible education to baccalaureate, master’s, and doctoral students. Assistant Professors are expected to engage in scholarly activities, teach undergraduate and graduate courses based on their qualifications, and demonstrate a commitment to OU, the SoN, and professional service.</div> 0090 - Nursing https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38912 2026-09-01T14:17:49-04:00 2026-09-01T14:17:50-04:00 Assistant Softball Coach <div>The Oakland University Assistant Softball Coach is responsible for assisting the head coach in developing a NCAA Division I softball program for student-athletes, within the rules and policies of The NCAA and Conference legislated guidelines. The assistant coach must also assist in the training and development of team/players on and off the field; liaison for academics and other departments on campus; Assist with travel arrangements and ordering of softball equipment.</div> 2836 - Athletics Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/33688 2025-02-06T10:22:10-05:00 2025-02-06T10:22:10-05:00 Advanced Behavior Technician <div>Supervise clients and staff during ABA therapy. To provide clinical support to senior staff, perform behavior technician roles on challenging behavior cases, increase reliable and needed staff when there are staff absences or vacations.</div><div><br><br></div> 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38605 2026-08-06T08:33:11-04:00 2026-08-06T08:33:11-04:00 Athletics Game Day Stats Assistant <div>The Gameday Stats Assistant serves as the official stats taker at live home athletic events to be distributed to GoldenGrizzlies.com, ESPN, NCAA, and other media entities. This role is responsible for taking/inputting accurate stats into the NCAA Livestats Genius software based on the live action in-game.</div> 2836 - Athletics Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37454 2026-04-15T14:38:20-04:00 2026-04-15T14:38:21-04:00 Standardized Patient <div>Under training and close supervision in a clinical education setting, consistently and accurately portrays specified emotional, behavioral and/or physical disease symptoms while interacting with health care students during simulated patient examinations designed to evaluate student experiential earning and or assessment of student progress.</div> 0101 - SOM - Medical Education https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38956 2026-09-04T15:59:56-04:00 2026-09-04T15:59:56-04:00 Associate Vice President and Controller <div>Provide strategic leadership and oversight for the University’s accounting services functions, which include responsibility for the University’s general ledger system, and related fund accounting practices. Lead and support directors across Central Accounting, Accounts Payable, Student Business Services, Payroll, and Purchasing. Direct the development and implementation of financial policies and procedures that promote operational excellence, high quality customer service, and robust compliance. Contribute to a results-oriented culture through collaboration with the Finance &amp; Administration leadership team. Serve as a key partner in constructive conflict resolution, continuous improvement, and the advancement of the University’s goals.</div> 4483 - Finance & Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38053 2026-06-10T16:31:28-04:00 2026-06-10T16:31:28-04:00 Athletics Ticket Staff <div>To act as the front-line ambassador of our organization by managing point-of-sale transactions during sporting events. The role is designed to ensure guests receive a welcoming, efficient, and seamless experience when purchasing tickets.</div> 2836 - Athletics Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38978 2026-09-04T17:29:20-04:00 2026-09-04T17:29:20-04:00 Office Assistant I <div>To perform a variety of multi-step clerical procedures required for the maintenance and support of a unit.</div> 3170 - Counseling Center https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36759 2026-01-16T10:33:58-05:00 2026-01-16T10:33:58-05:00 Project Manager <div>The Department of Human Development and Child Studies (HDCS), housed in the School of Education and Human Services, invites applications to a part-time project manager position to work on a grant funded study on Pre-K evaluation.<br><br></div><div><br><br></div> 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38936 2026-09-03T11:22:56-04:00 2026-09-03T11:22:57-04:00 Accounting Office Part-Time Team Member <div>Position performs research and provides recommendations on various GASB and tax-related issues. Prepares financial analyses, assists with year-end closing, financial statement preparation and external audits. Performs various investment administration activities. Prepares various Federal, state and local tax returns. Works on various projects and other duties as assigned. Provides advice and training to other team members.</div> 2445 - Accounting Office https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/33693 2025-02-06T10:23:58-05:00 2025-02-06T10:23:58-05:00 Pontiac Community Interviewer <div>The Oakland University-Pontiac Initiative, Early Childhood Education (OUPIECE) group and the Department of Human Development and Child Studies (HDCS) at Oakland University, in partnership with Pontiac School District (PSD) invite applications to the Pontiac Community Interviewer position to work on a newly funded project to co-design an infant-toddler center and resource hub at Pontiac High School (Baby PEACE).</div><div><strong><br></strong>El grupo de la Iniciativa Oakland University-Pontiac, Educación Infantil Temprana (OUPIECE) y el Departamento de Desarrollo Humano y Estudios Infantiles (HDCS) de la Universidad de Oakland, en asociación con el Distrito Escolar de Pontiac (PSD) invitan solicitantes para el puesto de Entrevistador de la Comunidad de Pontiac para trabajar en un proyecto recientemente financiado para co-diseñar un centro para bebés y niños pequeños y un centro de recursos en Pontiac High School (Baby PEACE).</div> 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38624 2026-08-06T16:53:48-04:00 2026-08-06T16:53:49-04:00 Tutoring Services Coordinator <div>The Tutoring Services Coordinator will report to the Director of Academic Success and will assist</div><div>in monitoring the academics for men’s and women’s basketball student-athletes as well as at-risk student-athletes from all sports.</div> 2836 - Athletics Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37562 2026-04-29T16:49:48-04:00 2026-04-29T16:49:49-04:00 Research Associate - Early Literacy <div>The Department of Human Development and Child Studies (HDCS), housed in the School of Education and Human Services, invites applications to a part-time Research Associate position to work on a newly funded research and evaluation project on Early Literacy coaching.</div> 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38958 2026-09-04T16:01:13-04:00 2026-09-04T16:01:14-04:00 Director of Title IX and Compliance <div>Responsible for investigating, reporting and training related to the following areas: Title IX, Equal Opportunity, and Americans with Disabilities Act and attendant duties.</div> 4811 - Chief of Staff https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38943 2026-09-04T15:32:10-04:00 2026-09-04T15:32:10-04:00 Core Infrastructure Engineer <div>University Technology Services, the central IT organization of Oakland University, is seeking a Core Services Engineer to perform technology tasks. The Core Services Engineer is responsible for the administration, maintenance, and optimization of the organization’s core infrastructure and collaboration platforms—with a primary focus on Google Workspace and supporting responsibilities for Microsoft 365 and cloud identity services - Microsoft Entra ID. This position ensures secure, reliable, and efficient delivery of essential IT services while driving automation, standardization, and continuous improvement. The Core Services Engineer collaborates across IT teams to enhance productivity, streamline operations, and ensure seamless integration between Google and Microsoft ecosystems. The role requires a deep understanding of email services, including troubleshooting, configuration, and optimization to support institutional communication needs.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong><br><br></div><ul><li>Serve as the primary administrator and subject matter expert for Google Workspace, including Gmail, Drive, Shared Drives, Groups, and collaboration services, ensuring secure, reliable, and high-performing operations.</li><li>Administer and maintain enterprise email services, including configuration, routing, security controls, troubleshooting, and performance optimization.</li><li>Support and maintain core services operating within cloud and hosted environments, ensuring reliability, security, and alignment with institutional standards.</li><li>Ensure the reliability, security, and performance of core collaboration and infrastructure services.</li><li>Perform routine system maintenance, including patching, updates, upgrades, and service monitoring to maintain system integrity and compliance.</li><li>Develop and maintain automation scripts, configuration standards, and operational documentation to improve efficiency and service consistency.</li><li>Lead or support system migrations, platform integrations, and service improvement initiatives related to collaboration and enterprise systems.</li><li>Participate in enterprise patch management and coordinate maintenance communications to minimize service disruption.</li><li>Collaborate with IT leadership and cross-functional teams to align core services with institutional needs and service standards.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>The best things about this position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>The teamwork; you are a member of a talented team.</li><li>The ability to learn and grow professionally. We provide many opportunities to continue to advance your knowledge and professional skills.</li><li>Your work matters to the students, faculty, and employees at the University.</li><li>The University offers an attractive benefits package that includes excellent healthcare and tuition benefits for employees and their families, flexible work schedules, paid vacation, wellness programs, friendly campus events, and generous retirement contributions.</li></ul> 2167 - University Technology Services https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38065 2026-06-12T10:25:27-04:00 2026-06-12T10:25:27-04:00 Athletics Facility Event Staff <div>The Facility Event Staff position supports the successful operation of Oakland University Athletics facilities and game-day events. This casual role assists with event setup and breakdown, guest services, facility preparation, crowd management, and operational support to ensure a safe, welcoming, and professional environment for student-athletes, coaches, officials, fans, and guests.<br><br></div><div>Facility Event Staff serve as representatives of Oakland University Athletics and play an important role in delivering a first-class event experience.</div> 2836 - Athletics Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38980 2026-09-04T17:30:38-04:00 2026-09-04T17:30:38-04:00 Laboratory Stockroom Coordinator <div>To be responsible for all of the departmental instructional laboratories. Coordinate laboratory activities including preparing solutions, setting up weekly experiments for all laboratory courses, ordering stockroom supplies, and ensuring that the equipment and facilities are in proper working condition.</div> 0305 - Biological Sciences https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36851 2026-01-30T16:02:05-05:00 2026-01-30T16:02:06-05:00 Greenskeeper <div>To assist in the maintenance operation of Oakland University’s 36 hole golfing facility.</div> 2465 - Golf Courses https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/34422 2025-04-01T14:00:16-04:00 2025-04-01T14:00:17-04:00 Farm Manager - Campus Student Organic Farm <div>Manage Campus Student Organic Farm personnel and help with the Campus Student Organic Farm success.</div> 0305 - Biological Sciences https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38721 2026-08-13T16:12:26-04:00 2026-08-13T16:12:26-04:00 OUCARES Sports Coach <div>Lead an OUCARES sports or social skills program with the goal of improving the quality of life of participants with Autism and their families.</div> 0917 - SEHS OUCARES https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37637 2026-05-11T08:28:00-04:00 2026-05-11T08:28:00-04:00 Substitute Teacher <div>The substitute teacher position exists on an \"as needed\" basis when Lowry<br>teachers and staff are not available.</div> 8837 - Lowry Center for Early Childhood https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38960 2026-09-04T16:02:24-04:00 2026-09-04T16:02:25-04:00 Executive Director of Treasury Management <div>Provide strategic leadership and oversight for the University’s treasury management functions, including debt administration, working capital investments, endowment investments, and related financial operations. Ensure the prudent stewardship of institutional financial resources through effective investment management, debt financing, liquidity planning, risk management, and policy development in support of the University’s mission, financial sustainability, and long-term strategic objectives.</div> 4483 - Finance & Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36975 2026-02-17T10:07:41-05:00 2026-02-17T10:07:42-05:00 Research Intern <div>To support faculty-led research activities through a supervised, temporary research internship.</div> 2064 - Computer Science & Engineering https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38945 2026-09-04T15:44:51-04:00 2026-09-04T15:44:51-04:00 OUWBSOM Manager for Corporate Relations <div>Reporting directly to the Sr. Director of Philanthropy OUWB SOM, the Manager of Corporate Relations will conduct Corporate gift fundraising activities for OUWB and the OU schools of Health. This is a unique position that will primarily manage a corporate portfolio. This position will manage the fundraising process for an assigned portfolio of prospects and donors and conducts activities leading to gifts of $25,000 and above for identified goals and programs. The candidate will be responsible for aspects of corporate fundraising for OUWB, SON and SHS which includes corporate research, sponsorship cultivation and solicitation, and sponsorship benefits fulfillment, and working with the corporate advancement team to support broad based solicitation strategies and projects.</div> 0100 - School of Medicine https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38123 2026-06-19T00:00:31-04:00 2026-06-19T00:00:32-04:00 Custodian <div>To perform cleaning activities and maintain assigned areas in various campus classroom and office buildings and on an emergency basis, perform grounds related tasks.</div> 5347 - Housing Facilities https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38982 2026-09-04T17:32:54-04:00 2026-09-04T17:32:54-04:00 Office Assistant III <div>To provide specialized office assistance, coordinating procedural business or service activities for a complex program area involving processing, implementing, advising on, and reporting specialized subject matter.</div> 1495 - Sociology, Anthropology, Social Work and Criminal Justice https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/34439 2025-04-02T12:52:48-04:00 2025-04-02T12:52:49-04:00 Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy <div>The Physical Therapy Program in the Department of Human Movement Science at Oakland University (Rochester, MI) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position starting August 15, 2025. This is a unique growth opportunity to join a supportive faculty with excellent resources, balancing teaching, research, and service.<br><br>Teaching: Contribute expertise across our Physical Therapy programs, including the Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT), graduate/post-professional certificates (Orthopedic Manual PT, Oncology Rehab, Teaching &amp; Learning), and Ph.D. in Human Movement Science.<br><br>Research: Receive support and mentorship to establish a peer-reviewed research agenda, leveraging state-of-the-art labs, clinical partnerships, and strengths in upstream care and community engagement.<br><br>Service: Strengthen relationships with clinical partners, contribute to student recruitment and retention, and enhance academic programs and professional organizations. Oakland University values an inclusive commitment to teaching, research, and service.<br><br>We encourage applications from individuals who can broaden and advance our strengths in foundational and clinical sciences. Those with board certifications orgraduate certificates are especially encouraged to apply.</div> 0738 - Human Movement Science https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38726 2026-08-14T10:21:02-04:00 2026-08-14T10:21:03-04:00 GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position: Clare-Gladwin Counties <div><strong>The Department of Human Development and Child Studies (HDCS), housed in the School of Education and Human Services, invites applications for several part-time Data Collector positions to work on a statewide preschool evaluation. We are seeking applicants available for 2–3 weekday mornings during preschool classroom hours in September–October and April–May to conduct in-person child assessments. Some afternoon and/or evening availability will also be needed to complete required post-assessment paperwork.</strong></div> 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37753 2026-05-15T14:49:54-04:00 2026-05-15T14:49:54-04:00 Meadow Brook Estate Museum Security Guard <div>Security of Meadow Brook Hall buildings, grounds, and collections.<br><br></div> 3760 - Meadow Brook Estate https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38962 2026-09-04T16:07:47-04:00 2026-09-04T16:07:48-04:00 Assistant General Counsel <div>Assist the General Counsel in providing legal services to the University on an extensive range of legal matters including without limitation general business, board governance, constitutional law, compliance, governmental immunity, intellectual property, patent, copyright, health care, labor and employment, employee benefits, tax, contracts, academic and policy issues, real estate and construction, bankruptcy, charter schools, immigration, privacy and data security, software agreements, planned giving, gifts, endowments, government regulations, charitable gaming, FOIA, HIPAA, COBRA, FERPA, Clery Act, FMLA, litigation, scientific research, police/criminal law, risk management, liquor license and other assigned areas and duties consistent with the skills, interests and needs of the office.</div> 4112 - Legal Affairs/Gen Counsel/Bd Of Trustees https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37059 2026-02-26T11:49:13-05:00 2026-02-26T11:49:13-05:00 Principal Faculty Oakland University Master of Physician Assistant Science Program; Assistant Professor of Practice <div>Principal Faculty are responsible for teaching, curriculum development, student assessment, and Program support across all phases of the Physician Assistant Program. Faculty contribute to the academic, professional, and accreditation-related functions of the Program in alignment with<br>ARC-PA Standards.</div> 0729 - Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38947 2026-09-04T15:46:36-04:00 2026-09-04T15:46:37-04:00 Financial Aid Adviser <div>Provide counseling and advice to students and parents about financial services, financial aid, financial literacy, student account and billing, payment plans and student employment. Process financial aid applications, including budgeting, packaging of awards, revising award, verification, and resolving conflicting information. Deliver exceptional customer service through various communication systems. Conduct workshops, seminars, presentations, etc. about financial assistance programs. Demonstrate integrity and ethical behavior in working with confidential information and maintain a high level of confidentiality.</div> 5131 - Office of Financial Aid and Scholarships https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38238 2026-06-29T10:39:16-04:00 2026-06-29T10:39:17-04:00 SECS Associate Dean for Research <div><strong>INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY.</strong><br><br>Provide leadership and manage the administrative aspects of the research activities in the School of Engineering and Computer Science .</div> 0050 - Engineering & Computer Science https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38964 2026-09-04T16:09:11-04:00 2026-09-04T16:09:12-04:00 Art & Practice of Medicine Course Coordinator <div>Reporting directly to the Director, Clinical Skills Training and Simulation, the SP Coordinator will provide administrative support for the Clinical Skills Center (CSC), located at the Troy campus of Beaumont Hospital. The coordinator will function as an initial point of contact for the CSC. The coordinator is responsible for administrative processes in the center including scheduling, purchasing, payroll, logistics, and record maintenance. The SP Coordinator will provide general oversight to the Standardized Patients.</div> 0100 - School of Medicine https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/35142 2025-06-06T08:19:08-04:00 2025-06-06T08:19:09-04:00 Wellness Assistant <div>Provide educational wellness workshops for students, faculty/staff and community members of the Oakland University community.</div> 5332 - University Recreation and Well-Being Fit. & Wellness https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38808 2026-08-21T08:53:32-04:00 2026-08-21T08:53:32-04:00 Development Associate - School of Health Sciences <div>The Development Associate (DA) will support and facilitate development office projects, excluding major gift work, for the School of Health Sciences. They will take responsibility for development functions including donor stewardship outreach and communications; annual fund efforts; supporting fundraising and donor engagement events; gift processing; and other development related efforts not directly linked to cultivating and soliciting major gifts. The DA is also responsible for writing and preparing executive level communication, custom acknowledgement letters, donor impact reports, and providing proposal writing support.<br><br>The DA will report to the Director of Philanthropy, School of Nursing &amp; School of Health Sciences and must have experience in managing multiple tasks and a good working knowledge ofdevelopment. Note: Evening and weekend hours may occasionally be required.</div> 0070 - Health Sciences https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37756 2026-05-18T09:14:52-04:00 2026-05-18T09:14:52-04:00 Visiting Faculty - Nursing <div>The Oakland University School of Nursing seeks multiple full-time Visiting Instructors for the 2026–2027 academic year. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses, clinical rotations, and/or lab/simulation based on expertise. Candidates must hold (or be eligible for) Michigan RN licensure and a master’s or doctoral degree in nursing. Preferred applicants will have specialty expertise in areas such as acute care, OB, pediatrics, mental health, leadership, or simulation, along with prior teaching experience. Strong communication skills, community engagement, and a demonstrated commitment to diversity and inclusion are essential.</div> 0090 - Nursing https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37224 2026-03-19T15:36:31-04:00 2026-03-19T15:36:31-04:00 Meadow Brook Estate Facility Operations Associate <div>The facility operations team is responsible for the physical care &amp; maintenance of the building and the preparation of rooms, event spaces and grounds for all programming at Meadow Brook Hall.</div> 3760 - Meadow Brook Estate https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38949 2026-09-04T15:51:35-04:00 2026-09-04T15:51:36-04:00 Manager of Electrical and Plumbing Department <div>Plan, organize and supervise facility maintenance and services dealing with building electrical, plumbing, and elevator components and systems.</div> 4300 - Facilities Management https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38281 2026-07-02T11:56:23-04:00 2026-07-02T11:56:24-04:00 Temp IT Financial/Budget Analyst 2167 - University Technology Services https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37876 2026-05-26T16:37:38-04:00 2026-05-26T16:37:38-04:00 Visiting Instructor of Mathematics and Statistics <div>The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Oakland University invites applications for at least one Visiting Instructor position. The successful candidate will primarily be responsible for supporting the department’s teaching mission through the instruction of foundational undergraduate courses (including introductory mathematics and statistics).<br><br></div><div>The standard teaching load for this position is three courses per semester (3+3). In addition to teaching excellence, the Visiting Instructor is required to fulfill service duties that advance the department's mission. These may include assisting with student success initiatives. As this is a teaching-intensive appointment, there are no research requirements or expectations for scholarly publication.<br><br></div> 1038 - Mathematical & Statistics https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38966 2026-09-04T16:10:07-04:00 2026-09-04T16:10:08-04:00 Assistant Director <div>Provide leadership and management for university-sponsored college access and readiness programs that expand educational opportunities and promote postsecondary success for pre-college students. Assists with the planning, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of federally, state, and university-funded pre-college initiatives while ensuring compliance with grant requirements and institutional policies. Provide direct training and supervision to graduate assistants, undergraduate student tutors and mentors. Collaborates with university, K–12, community, and external partners to support college awareness, academic achievement, career exploration, family engagement, and successful transitions to higher education through data-informed decision-making and strategic partnerships.</div> 2140 - Pre-College Programs https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/35983 2025-09-03T13:30:41-04:00 2025-09-03T13:30:42-04:00 Assistant/Associate Professor for Environmental Health and Safety <div>The Department of Public and Environmental Wellness in the School of Health Sciences at Oakland University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in Environmental Health and Safety (EHS). The successful candidate will join a dynamic and multidisciplinary department committed to excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement.</div><div><br></div><div>We seek a candidate who will initiate and maintain a successful program of research, scholarship, and service. The ideal candidate will contribute to both undergraduate and graduate instruction in Environmental Health and Safety, support the department’s mission, and actively engage in curriculum development and program growth.<br><br>Responsibilities include:</div><ul><li>Developing and sustaining an active ​scholarship agenda in Environmental Health and Safety or a related field</li><li>Teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses in EHS and related topics</li><li>Engaging in service to the department, college, university, and professional communities</li><li>Advising and mentoring students</li><li>Contributing to program development, improvement, and accreditation activities</li><li>Participating in community engagement initiatives and, where appropriate, program leadership</li></ul> 1034 - Public and Environmental Wellness https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38864 2026-08-27T00:00:11-04:00 2026-08-27T00:00:13-04:00 Greenskeeper <div>Under the direction of the Head and Assistant Golf Course Superintendent, maintain the primary golf course playing surfaces and landscaped areas.</div> 2465 - Golf Courses https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37300 2026-03-27T15:31:51-04:00 2026-03-27T15:31:51-04:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Physical Therapy <div>The Physical Therapy Program in the Department of Human Movement Science at Oakland University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor position beginning August 15, 2026.<br><br></div><div>We seek a dynamic educator–scholar committed to advancing physical therapy education, clinical practice, and translational research. The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty within the School of Health Sciences and contribute to teaching in the Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) curriculum while developing a program of scholarship supported by strong clinical partnerships, research infrastructure, and mentorship opportunities.<br><br></div> 0738 - Human Movement Science https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38951 2026-09-04T15:52:31-04:00 2026-09-04T15:52:32-04:00 Admissions Adviser <div>Ensure that prospective students are recruited, admitted, and oriented to the university and assist in the facilitation of recruitment, yield, and transition programs.</div> 2609 - Admissions https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38349 2026-07-13T09:36:28-04:00 2026-07-13T09:36:28-04:00 Meadow Brook Estate Business Office Assistant <div>To support MBE Associate Director of Administration and Finance with a variety of bookkeeping tasks, reconciliations, reports, and schedules. Support event operation with alcohol inventory management and retail sales operation with cash management and reconciliation.</div> 3760 - Meadow Brook Estate https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37927 2026-06-01T08:49:20-04:00 2026-06-01T08:49:20-04:00 Assistant Professor of Writing & Rhetoric - Writing across the Curriculum <div>The Department of Writing and Rhetoric seeks applicants specializing in writing across the curriculum for a tenure-track Assistant Professor to begin immediately on August 15, 2026. The ideal candidate will possess a research and instructional agenda in writing across the curriculum and/or writing in the disciplines. This colleague will teach courses in the Department’s award-winning Professional and Digital Writing major and writing minor, as well as our award-winning first-year writing program. Writing Center tutoring and administrative experience are preferred to advance our ongoing partnership with the university’s Writing Center. Additionally, the new colleague is expected to lead professional development within the department and across the university on topics such as writing across the curriculum, information literacy, and undergraduate research. The colleague will also serve on vital department, college, and university committees. Interest in and experience with community engagement, especially K-12 outreach, are preferred to help the university advance its recent designation as a Carnegie Community Engaged campus. PhD in Rhetoric and Composition, Writing Studies, or related discipline such as English or Education is required. Expected teaching assignment is 3/2.</div> 1663 - Writing and Rhetoric https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38968 2026-09-04T16:10:56-04:00 2026-09-04T16:10:57-04:00 Assistant Director of Advising <div>As the School of Nursing (SON) has continued to grow, so has the number of advisers and programs. The Assistant Director of Advising will be responsible for the day-to-day operational needs for advising services. The Assistant Director will be instrumental in developing and supporting targeted initiatives aimed at enhancing nursing-specific orientations, registration, academic progress, and overall academic success. In addition to managing an advising caseload, the Assistant Director will focus on increasing the retention and success of both graduate and undergraduate nursing students. The Assistant Director will support the Director in leading initiatives to enhance our advising services, ensuring that all students receive personalized guidance throughout their academic journey.<br><br></div> 0090 - Nursing https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36331 2025-10-23T11:11:13-04:00 2025-10-23T11:11:13-04:00 Assistant Professor <div>We seek applicants with research and teaching interests related to robotics, with a focus on mechanical design, materials, autonomy, AI, and control systems. Successful candidates will be expected to develop an externally funded research program that includes fundamental and/or applied research. The candidate should be able to teach and develop courses in robotics related subjects at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. An earned doctorate in Mechanical or a closely related field is required.</div> 2102 - Mechanical Engineering https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38887 2026-08-28T11:54:00-04:00 2026-08-28T11:54:01-04:00 Course Design Assistant <div>The Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning (CETL) is seeking a motivated and innovative individual to assist our team in building engaging, self-paced online learning opportunities for educational development programs. The ideal candidate is a recent graduate with foundational experience in instructional design who will help develop online modules, create organizational templates, and support digital accessibility efforts. This position is essential in contributing to the center's mission of fostering inclusive and effective teaching practices.</div> 2163 - Center for Excellence in Teaching/Learning https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37302 2026-03-27T15:58:36-04:00 2026-03-27T15:58:37-04:00 Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Public Health <div>The Department of Public and Environmental Wellness invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Public Health. We seek a scholar with an established or emerging program of externally funded research that advances contemporary public health practice and policy within an interdisciplinary department integrating Public Health and Environmental Health and Safety.<br><br>Areas of interest include, but are not limited to:<br><br>● Health policy, administration, and management<br>● Public health systems, policy analysis and implementation, and program evaluation<br>● Prevention science<br>● Population health<br>● Implementation and translational science<br>● Data-informed public health decision-making<br>● Leadership roles in newly formed academic programs<br><br>The successful candidate will:<br>● Maintain a productive, externally funded research program with a clear trajectory toward sustained grant activity<br>● Contribute to interdisciplinary research initiatives linking population health, implementation, and translational science with policy development and evaluation<br>● Teach undergraduate and/or graduate public health courses, including health policy and management and related core content<br>● Develop advanced electives aligned with research expertise<br>● Mentor students in research and applied public health practice<br>● Engage in service at the department, university, and professional levels<br><br></div> 1034 - Public and Environmental Wellness https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38953 2026-09-04T15:55:42-04:00 2026-09-04T15:55:43-04:00 Coordinator for Learning Communities <div>The Coordinator for Learning Communities develops and coordinates residential learning initiatives that support student engagement, academic success, and community building. Through collaboration with faculty, campus partners, and Housing staff, this position creates and assesses programs and experiences that promote student learning, belonging, and retention while providing support for student staff and residential community participants.</div> 3118 - Housing Residential Life https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38543 2026-07-30T09:20:25-04:00 2026-07-30T09:20:26-04:00 Wellness Ambassador <div>A Wellness Ambassador assists with promoting and supporting the overall health and well-being of students, faculty, and staff by encouraging participation in wellness programs and initiatives. This role involves educating the campus community about available resources, wellness opportunities, and healthy lifestyle choices through in-person interactions, events, and digital platforms. The Wellness Ambassador will assist in organizing wellness events, activities, and campaigns, fostering a positive and supportive environment for physical, mental, and emotional health. They will serve as a resource, providing information, guidance, and support to help individuals reach their wellness goals.</div> 5332 - University Recreation and Well-Being Fit. & Wellness https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38011 2026-06-09T08:44:18-04:00 2026-06-09T08:44:19-04:00 STEM Summer Camp Counselor <div>Oakland University School or Engineering and Computer Science (SECS) Outreach Department is committed to STEM education for Kindergarten though 12th grade students.<br><br>Our SECS Outreach Department is looking for a highly organized, driven, cheerful, and detailed-oriented individual to fill the position of STEM Summer Camp High School Counselor. This position reports directly to the Assistant Director of Outreach and Retention.</div> 0050 - Engineering & Computer Science https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38970 2026-09-04T16:11:49-04:00 2026-09-04T16:11:50-04:00 Physician Assistant Program Coordinator <div>The Physician Assistant (PA) Program Coordinator provides administrative, operational, andlogistical support to the Physician Assistant Program. The Program Coordinator ensuresefficient day-to-day operations while supporting compliance with accreditation standards,university policies, and program objectives. This position requires a highly organized, proactiveindividual who excels in planning, communication, problem-solving, and project management.</div> 0729 - Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36362 2025-10-29T16:31:44-04:00 2025-10-29T16:31:45-04:00 Assistant Professor of Accounting <div>The Department of Accounting and Finance in the School of Business Administration at Oakland University is recruiting an assistant professor to teach undergraduate and graduate level courses in Accounting and to maintain a high level of quality research and service activities. For this appointment, candidates must have a Ph.D. in accounting or equivalent from an AACSB accredited institution (advanced ABD status considered), and evidence of scholarly achievement or potential, and quality teaching. Desired Qualifications: • All research and teaching areas will be considered, analytics, auditing and assurance services preferred • Evidence of scholarly activity that has positively impacted academic or professional audiences, • Evidence of effective Masters of Accounting, M.B.A. or equivalent teaching experience, • Leadership experience or an interest in taking on leadership responsibilities, • Relevant professional accounting and/or industry experience, • Possession of professional accounting certification, • Evidence of successful interactions with the professional community, • Evidence of obtaining external funding, • Ability to effectively collaborate with other faculty members, and • Experience/interest in Global/International aspects of Accounting.</div> 0460 - Accounting & Finance https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38898 2026-08-28T14:57:28-04:00 2026-08-28T14:57:29-04:00 Development Associate - School of Nursing <div>The Development Associate (DA) will support and facilitate development office projects, excluding major gift work, for the School of Nursing. They will take responsibility for development functions including donor stewardship outreach and communications; annual fund efforts; supporting fundraising and donor engagement events; gift processing; and other development related efforts not directly linked to cultivating and soliciting major gifts. The DA is also responsible for writing and preparing executive level communication, custom acknowledgement letters, donor impact reports, and providing proposal writing support.<br><br></div><div>The DA will report to the Director of Philanthropy, School of Nursing &amp; School of Health Sciences and must have experience in managing multiple tasks and a good working knowledge of development. Note: Evening and weekend hours may occasionally be required.</div> 0090 - Nursing https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38603 2026-08-06T08:29:05-04:00 2026-08-06T08:29:06-04:00 Assistant Director of Annual Giving <div>The Assistant Director of Annual Giving provides the implementation and coordination of the Oakland University Fund Drive (faculty, staff, retiree giving campaign), yearly direct mail campaigns, the Parent Program, and student initiatives such as the Senior Class Gift, Senior Tower Climb and Student Philanthropy Committee.</div><div><br></div><div>In addition, the Assistant Director of Annual Giving manages a small focused Leadership Annual Giving donor portfolio.</div><div><br></div><div>The position handles specialized operational tasks, such as memorial bench procurement and providing Giving Day support.</div> 3548 - Annual Giving https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37443 2026-04-14T14:21:40-04:00 2026-04-14T14:21:40-04:00 Special Instructor in Public and Environmental Wellness <div>The Department of Public and Environmental Wellness seeks a Special Instructor to provide high-impact undergraduate and graduate instruction and service within the programs of Public Health and Environmental Health and Safety. This is a teaching-focused appointment without research responsibilities.<br><br></div><div>This role is designed to strengthen education through excellence in communication, student engagement, and applied public health instruction while supporting accreditation-aligned competency development.<br><br></div><div><strong>Primary responsibilities include:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Teaching health communication and related courses required to maintain accreditations</li><li>Mentoring students to support academic progression and workforce readiness</li><li>Contributing to curriculum implementation, assessment, and continuous quality improvement processes</li><li>Establishing, coordinating, and evaluating student internships / practicums</li><li>Supporting community-engaged learning initiatives and experiential education partnerships</li><li>Participating in service activities at the program, department, school, and university levels</li></ul><div><br></div><div>The successful candidate will demonstrate strong communication skills, organizational effectiveness, and the ability to help students learn to translate foundational health principles and deliver them precisely and effectively to all audiences.<br><br></div> 1034 - Public and Environmental Wellness https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38955 2026-09-04T15:58:47-04:00 2026-09-04T15:58:48-04:00 Testing Coordinator/ Disability Coordinator <div>This hybrid role supports the mission of the Disability Support Services (DSS) office by coordinating accommodated testing services (75%) and performing disability intake and accommodation assessments (25%). Reviews and processes all exam appointment requests submitted by students and communicates follow-up questions as needed. Manages faculty communications related to student exam appointments. Facilitates the administration and proctoring of exams for students registered with Disability Support Services, including weekly evening hours. Oversees the secure receipt, handling, storage, and return of exams to safeguard the integrity and confidentiality of testing materials. Assists the Director with data collection and reporting related to the testing process. Designs and presents programs to educate and sensitize the OU community about the needs of students with disabilities. Coordinates appropriate academic adjustments, reasonable accommodations and other services for students with disabilities. Evaluates disability documentation to determine student eligibility for academic adjustments, reasonable accommodations and other services. Consult with faculty and other campus administrative areas to facilitate student disability related services and accommodations. Explains University services, policy and procedures to students and parents during intake appointments.</div> 3210 - Disability Support Services https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38051 2026-06-10T16:19:03-04:00 2026-06-10T16:19:03-04:00 Athletics Broadcast Assistant <div>To provide a specialized and technical skillset for our live sports productions.</div> 2836 - Athletics Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38977 2026-09-04T17:28:43-04:00 2026-09-04T17:28:43-04:00 Accounts Payable Coordinator <div>Coordinates payment documents being received by Accounts Payable, accurately assessing compliance to OU policies and other related requirements, completing the weekly payment run with payments being processed timely and accurately in conjunction with established policies and procedures.</div> 4765 - Accounts Payable https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36679 2025-12-19T08:45:41-05:00 2025-12-19T08:45:42-05:00 CRNA Instructor of Practice <div>The Oakland University School of Nursing is seeking a highly motivated and qualified CRNA applicant to teach graduate students enrolled in the Oakland University-Beaumont Graduate Program of Nurse Anesthesia, beginning August 15, 2026.<br><br>Applicants will be expected to engage in all aspects of the program, including but not limited to teaching in the classroom, clinical mentoring, guiding the development of clinical doctorate projects, and developing and evaluating curriculum. A minimum of two years in a leadership or faculty role is preferred.<br><br>Candidates must be expert clinicians and able to demonstrate an ongoing commitment to service. The ability to effectively communicate and work within a team environment is essential. First consideration will be given to applicants who apply by March 15, 2026, with the continued search until the position is filled. After March 15, it is highly recommended you reach out to the committee chair via email if you are considering applying to learn where we are in the search process.</div> 0090 - Nursing https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38932 2026-09-03T00:00:12-04:00 2026-09-03T00:00:13-04:00 Electrician <div>The successful candidate will be part of a skilled trades team responsible for campus-wide maintenance activities.</div> 4300 - Facilities Management https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/33689 2025-02-06T10:22:36-05:00 2025-02-06T10:22:36-05:00 Registered Nurse <div>Represent Graham Health Center in providing healthcare services and education to the OU campus community during outreach services and programs.</div> 3303 - Graham Health Center https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38608 2026-08-06T08:57:15-04:00 2026-08-06T08:57:15-04:00 Admissions Application Reader <div>Admissions Application Readers will recommend which applicants should advance in the admissions process to the Oakland University William Beaumont School of Medicine. Readers will holistically review written application materials, carefully evaluate academic preparation, assess an applicant’s exposure to the medical profession, as well as their desire to serve others and their communities.</div> 0100 - School of Medicine https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37475 2026-04-20T10:10:41-04:00 2026-04-20T10:10:41-04:00 Meadow Brook Estate Visitor Services Assistant 3760 - Meadow Brook Estate https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38957 2026-09-04T16:00:50-04:00 2026-09-04T16:00:51-04:00 Communications Manager, Office of the Provost <div>The Communications Manager serves as the primary communications resource for Academic Affairs—owning the day-to-day execution of the Provost’s communications plan while also bringing strategic judgment and independent initiative to the role.</div><div><br>This is a standalone embedded position. The Communications Manager operates with a high degree of autonomy, managing the full scope of Academic Affairs communications: executive content for the Provost, internal communications across schools and colleges, digital channel management, brand stewardship, and coordination with UCM’s central teams. The Manager is the sole dedicated communications professional for one of the university’s most complex and high-visibility leadership offices, and will act as a trusted liaison, ensuring all communications are handled with confidentiality and professional discretion.</div><div><br>The ideal candidate brings both strong execution skills and the professional maturity to work independently in a senior leadership environment, advise the Provost on communications decisions, and serve as a credible representative of UCM’s standards across the Academic Affairs community.</div> 7159 - Communications & Marketing https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38939 2026-09-03T15:33:38-04:00 2026-09-03T15:33:38-04:00 Tenure-track Assistant Professors of Computer Science <div><strong>The Department of Computer Science and Engineering needs to fill one tenure-track assistant professor position.<br><br></strong>The department is looking for candidates in the broad areas of Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, Data Science, and Computer Systems, although outstanding candidates in other related areas will also be considered. The position will begin on August 15, 2026. Candidates must show exceptional promise in both research and teaching.</div> 2064 - Computer Science & Engineering https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38054 2026-06-10T16:32:31-04:00 2026-06-10T16:32:31-04:00 Host/Hostess - VIP & Donor Rooms <div>The Host/Hostess serves as the first point of contact for donors, sponsors, alumni, university leadership, and special guests attending Oakland University Athletics events. This position is responsible for creating a welcoming and professional atmosphere within VIP and donor hospitality areas while providing exceptional customer service and ensuring guests have an outstanding game-day experience.</div> 2836 - Athletics Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38979 2026-09-04T17:29:50-04:00 2026-09-04T17:29:51-04:00 Office Assistant III <div>To provide specialized office assistance, coordinating procedural business or service activities for a complex program area involving processing, implementing, advising on, and reporting specialized subject matter.</div> 0729 - Clinical and Diagnostic Sciences https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36846 2026-01-30T10:12:19-05:00 2026-01-30T10:12:20-05:00 Senior Associate Dean of Academic Affairs <div><strong>Oakland University has retained the Executive Search Firm, Academic Search, to lead the search efforts. Interested applicants should visit the following link to see the advertisement with application instructions:&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.academicsearch.org/open-searches-public/entry/24500/?search=24500\"><strong>https://www.academicsearch.org/open-searches-public/entry/24500/?search=24500</strong></a></div> 0100 - School of Medicine https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/34328 2025-03-21T15:46:05-04:00 2025-03-21T15:46:05-04:00 Behavioral Therapist- ABA Clinic <div>This position is needed for students who have finished coursework but still needs hours, for summer staff who are accepted into the MEd but program begins in Fall, for BCaBA students that are enrolled in PACE courses/ Certificate programs and for students not enrolled at least half</div> 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38661 2026-08-11T10:37:30-04:00 2026-08-11T10:37:30-04:00 Communications Specialist <div>Help guide development of departmental communications; and marketing - primarily via social media platforms such as Instagram and LinkedIn.</div> 0305 - Biological Sciences https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37573 2026-05-01T11:23:18-04:00 2026-05-01T11:23:19-04:00 Visiting Assistant Professor in Early Elementary Education <div>The Early Childhood Education area in the Department of Human Development and Child Studies (HDCS) at Oakland University invites applications for a non-tenure-track, Visiting Assistant Professor position to begin in August 2026. We are especially interested in a candidate with expertise in early elementary education. The position is a one-year contract with the possibility of extension.</div><div><br></div><div>Responsibilities include teaching, mentoring, and supervising undergraduate and graduate students; providing service to the department, school, and university, as well as contributing to Oakland University’s mission for community partnerships and engagement.</div><div><br></div><div>For full consideration, please submit your completed application, along with the following required materials, by Friday, May 29, 2026. The position will be open until filled.</div><div><br><br></div> 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38959 2026-09-04T16:01:43-04:00 2026-09-04T16:01:44-04:00 Video Support Technician <div>The <strong>Video Support Technician</strong> supports the university’s strategic marketing and communications efforts through the creation of high-quality video and audio content while providing operational support for the Creative Media Team’s production facilities. Responsibilities include filming, video editing, podcast production, sound design, and supporting the production of campus events.</div><div>The position collaborates with senior video staff, creative team members, and account managers to deliver brand-aligned content and assist across all aspects of multimedia production. In addition, the Video Support Technician serves as the primary operator of the university’s podcast studio and helps maintain studio spaces and production equipment, ensuring cameras, lighting, audio, and related resources are organized, functional, and ready for use.</div> 7159 - Communications & Marketing https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38944 2026-09-04T15:35:01-04:00 2026-09-04T15:35:02-04:00 Assistant Athletic Director for Compliance <div>To coordinate athletic rules and compliance for the athletic department. Serve as part of the Departments administrative team.</div> 4112 - Legal Affairs/Gen Counsel/Bd Of Trustees https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38085 2026-06-16T13:05:46-04:00 2026-06-16T13:05:47-04:00 Athletics Public Address (PA) Announcer <div>The Public Address (PA) Announcer serves as the voice of Oakland University Athletics during live home athletic events. This role is responsible for delivering clear, energetic, and professional in-game announcements that enhance the fan experience and support game operations across multiple sports.</div> 2836 - Athletics Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38981 2026-09-04T17:32:22-04:00 2026-09-04T17:32:23-04:00 Research Information Clerk II <div>To maintain data files in the Office of Institutional Research; prepare research runs, assist in performance analyses and coordinate office operations.</div> 2669 - Institutional Research https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36906 2026-02-06T16:06:47-05:00 2026-02-06T16:06:48-05:00 Visiting Instructor ISE Department <div>A visiting faculty position with a general focus on Smart Manufacturing and related topics. The successful candidate will primarily contribute to teaching, curriculum development,and student engagement in areas aligned with smart and advanced manufacturing while supporting the department's mission in education, industry collaboration and applied research in all areas of Industrial and Systems Engineering.</div> 2095 - Industrial & Systems Engineering https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/34424 2025-04-01T14:05:03-04:00 2025-04-01T14:05:04-04:00 Farm Assistant - Campus Student Organic Farm <div>Help with the continued success of the Campus Student Organic Farm.</div> 0305 - Biological Sciences https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38722 2026-08-13T16:19:39-04:00 2026-08-13T16:19:40-04:00 GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position: Washtenaw County 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37739 2026-05-15T09:38:54-04:00 2026-05-15T09:38:55-04:00 IT Support Specialist/Asset Management <div>This role ensures the university maintains accurate visibility and control over its IT assets, enabling cost efficiency, security compliance, and strategic planning across the institution.<br><br>This position supports the UTS Active Directory migration project for the campus. This position will be will be responsible for all Device Lifecycle, Asset Management and Endpoint Device Management. This role ensures accurate tracking, compliance, and optimization of IT assets specifically using the IT Service Management (TDX) and Microsoft Intune software platforms.</div><div><br>This position plays a critical role in maintaining data integrity across asset inventories, supporting procurement and lifecycle planning, and aligning asset management practices with university policies, security standards, and financial accountability.</div> 0570 - UTS Help Desk and Desktop Services https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38961 2026-09-04T16:04:34-04:00 2026-09-04T16:04:35-04:00 Grants & Contracts Officer <div>Under general supervision, administers and facilitates grant preparation, submission, and post-award management for university faculty. Advises and assists departments with process and compliance issues related to funding agency regulations and standards, and oversees adherence to university administrative, fiscal, and accounting policies and procedures related to grants and contracts.</div> 2701 - Office of Research Administration https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37030 2026-02-24T16:44:24-05:00 2026-02-24T16:44:24-05:00 Infant/Toddler Director/Teacher <div>The Infant/Toddler Director/Teacher will oversee the daily operations and strategic direction of the Baby PEACE Infant Toddler Center and Resource Hub, ensuring high-quality care and educational experiences for infants and toddlers. The Director/Teacher will report to the Advisory Board, and work collaboratively with families, school staff, and community partners to foster a nurturing and inclusive environment. Work hours will vary until September 2026 at which time, we anticipate the position to become full-time (30-40 hours/week).<br><br></div><div>Prior to hire, the Infant-Toddler Teacher/Director must complete criminal background screening, drug screening, the State of Michigan Licensing Background check and fingerprinting, and a TB test with physician’s signature.<br><br></div><div><br><br></div> 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38946 2026-09-04T15:46:04-04:00 2026-09-04T15:46:05-04:00 Executive Director, Enrollment Marketing <div>Oakland University invites applications for a newly established Executive Director, Enrollment Marketing — a senior leader responsible for driving enrollment outcomes through integrated, data-driven marketing strategy. Reporting to the Chief Marketing and Communications Officer (CMCO) and working in close partnership with the Vice President for Enrollment Management, this role owns the university’s enrollment marketing performance — translating enrollment goals into integrated campaigns that drive inquiry, application, yield, and matriculation.</div><div>This is a high-visibility, high-impact position for a marketing leader who can operate at both a strategic and executive level — connecting brand, campaigns, CRM, and analytics into a cohesive system that delivers measurable results. The Executive Director will oversee agency performance, align marketing and enrollment priorities, and build a more accountable, data-driven approach to recruitment marketing across the university.</div> 7159 - Communications & Marketing https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38137 2026-06-19T10:50:16-04:00 2026-06-19T10:50:17-04:00 Custodian <div>To perform cleaning activities and maintain assigned areas in various campus classroom and office buildings and on an emergency basis, perform grounds related tasks.</div> 5347 - Housing Facilities https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38963 2026-09-04T16:08:34-04:00 2026-09-04T16:08:35-04:00 Medical School Curriculum Coordinator <div>Reports to the Curriculum Program Administrator for the Office of Medical Education. The Medical School Curriculum Coordinator will provide administrative support for curricular programs across all four years of the undergraduate medical education program of the Oakland University William Beaumont School of Medicine.</div> 0100 - School of Medicine https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/34963 2025-05-20T08:34:55-04:00 2025-05-20T08:34:55-04:00 Visiting Instructor of Counseling <div>The Department of Counseling at Oakland University, Rochester, Michigan is seeking applicants for a 1-year Visiting Faculty Position (School Counseling preferred or Clinical Mental Health). The position is a full-time appointment starting August 15, 2025. Responsibilities include teaching, research, and service activities. The Department of Counseling values high-quality teaching, research, and service and is committed to social justice, diversity, equity, and inclusion. The primary responsibilities of the position include:<br><br></div><div>Teach courses (3/3) at the masters and doctoral-levels<br><br></div><ul><li>Teach across the CACREP curriculum, including clinical courses</li><li>Advise students</li><li>Engage with curriculum planning and development<br><br></li></ul><div>Service<br><br></div><ul><li>Engage in service assignments at the Department, School, and/or University level</li><li>Engage in program accreditation</li><li>Engage in professional leadership within the counseling profession<br><br></li></ul> 1770 - Counseling https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38742 2026-08-17T16:48:50-04:00 2026-08-17T16:48:50-04:00 Bag Drop 2465 - Golf Courses https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37755 2026-05-18T09:05:22-04:00 2026-05-18T09:05:22-04:00 Special Instructor in Chemistry <div>The Department of Chemistry at Oakland University invites applications for a full-time faculty position in chemistry, with an anticipated start date of August 15, 2026. The appointment at the rank of Special Instructor is a full-time, teaching-focused faculty position that leads to job security equivalent to tenure. Special Instructors are expected to teach three courses (or the equivalent) during both the Fall and Winter semesters and to contribute to departmental service.</div><div><br>The department offers courses that support a wide range of majors and programs, including Chemistry, Biology, Health Sciences, Biomedical Sciences, and Engineering. The successful candidate will be expected to teach introductory/foundational lecture and laboratory courses within the chemistry curriculum. Potential teaching assignments include general chemistry, analytical chemistry, and related chemistry courses aligned with departmental needs and the candidate’s expertise. Opportunities for additional compensation may be available through summer teaching assignments during the May–August term.</div> 0542 - Chemistry https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37076 2026-03-02T12:57:36-05:00 2026-03-02T12:57:36-05:00 Oakland GSRP Evaluation Data Collector Position <div>The Department of Human Development and Child Studies (HDCS), housed in the School of Education and Human Services, invites applications for several part-time Data Collector positions to work on a newly funded statewide preschool evaluation. The Data Collectors will be required to work a total of 20-30 flexible weekday hours between the months of April - May (total across both months) to conduct in-person child assessments.<br><br>Prior to hire, the Oakland GSRP Evaluation Data Collector must complete criminal background screening, drug screening, the State of Michigan Licensing Background check and fingerprinting, and a TB test with physician’s signature.</div> 2055 - Human Development & Child Study https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38948 2026-09-04T15:47:59-04:00 2026-09-04T15:48:00-04:00 Security Coordinator <div>This position is responsible for maintaining a safe and secure environment for patrons and employees of Meadow Brook Hall by establishing and enforcing security policies and procedures and monitoring the premises and personnel.</div> 3760 - Meadow Brook Estate https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38257 2026-06-30T00:00:37-04:00 2026-06-30T00:00:38-04:00 Stationary Engineer/Boiler Operator (CHP) <div>The successful candidate will become part of a skilled trade’s team responsible for the Central Heating Plant (CHP) and campus-wide maintenance activities. This individual will be called upon to perform a variety of tasks associated with maintaining and operating CHP, High Temperature Hot Water (HTHW) distribution system, building HVAC, and various mechanical / plumbing / electrical/ control systems.</div> 4977 - Central Heating Plant https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37875 2026-05-26T16:30:14-04:00 2026-05-26T16:30:14-04:00 Visiting Assistant Professor of Art History <div>The Department of Art, Art History and Design at Oakland University invites candidates to apply for the position of Visiting Professor of Art History to begin August 15 2026. The area of specialization is open. Preference will be given to candidates specializing in Modern and Contemporary Art. A Ph.D. in art history or a qualified proximate field is required. The ideal candidate would be strongly devoted to undergraduate education and student success, and engaged in conducting innovative research in their field of expertise.<br><br></div><div>This position carries a six course teaching load per academic year. Teaching responsibilities include introductory surveys, upper-level courses in one’s areas of specialization, and methodology courses. We seek an educator who can generate broad interest among undergraduate general education students in lower-level survey courses and can inspire specific interest in upper-level courses in their areas of specialization. Upper-level courses should appeal to students of art history, graphic design, and studio art. The ability to teach the history and theory of graphic design would be an asset.<br><br></div><div>Full consideration will be given to applications received by June 26. We will conduct interviews via videoconferencing.<br><br>This is a one year position, potentially renewable.</div> 0138 - Art, Art History and Design https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38965 2026-09-04T16:09:41-04:00 2026-09-04T16:09:41-04:00 Compliance Coordinator <div>To assist the Assistant Athletic Director for Compliance, who reports to the General Counsel, in the coordination of athletic rules and NCAA compliance for Oakland University intercollegiate athletics. All duties must be performed in a manner consistent with NCAA, conference and Oakland University rules, regulations, ordinances, policies, procedures and guidelines.</div> 4112 - Legal Affairs/Gen Counsel/Bd Of Trustees https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/35170 2025-06-10T10:49:08-04:00 2025-06-10T10:49:08-04:00 Assistant Professor of Finance <div>The School of Business Administration at Oakland University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Finance, beginning August 15, 2026. Qualified candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Finance or a closely related field from an accredited institution by the time of appointment. Applicants should demonstrate the ability to produce high-quality scholarly research and a commitment to excellence in teaching. Faculty members in the Finance area teach at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. The standard teaching load allows for meaningful research engagement, and the school offers competitive salaries along with excellent fringe benefits. Candidates with expertise across all areas of finance are encouraged to apply, although preference is likely to be given to those with demonstrated teaching expertise in financial analytics.</div> 0460 - Accounting & Finance https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38860 2026-08-26T15:40:03-04:00 2026-08-26T15:40:04-04:00 Assistant Professor of Political Science - American Politics <div>The Department of Political Science at Oakland University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in American Politics at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning August 15, 2027.</div><div>We seek a candidate broadly trained in American Politics with an active research agenda and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching. The area of specialization within American Politics is open. The successful candidate will be expected to teach an introductory course in American politics and upper-division courses in political behavior and/or political institutions (other than the judiciary), as well as courses in the candidate’s areas of expertise. The ability to contribute to the department’s research methods sequence is highly desirable. Oakland University operates on the semester system, and the standard teaching load is five courses per academic year.</div> 1346 - Political Science https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37228 2026-03-20T09:45:21-04:00 2026-03-20T09:45:22-04:00 OUCARES Social Group Facilitator <div>Lead social program development and implementation with the goal of improving the quality of life of autistic participants and their families</div> 0917 - SEHS OUCARES https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38950 2026-09-04T15:52:06-04:00 2026-09-04T15:52:07-04:00 Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support <div>The Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support in the Office of the Registrar plays a key role in advancing the university’s commitment to student success. This position designs, develops, implements, and maintains digital processes, reports, and dashboards in accordance with established best practices, ensuring data integrity and reliability. The Assistant Registrar for Data and Systems Support develops and maintains comprehensive process documentation to support accuracy and consistency, and provides staff training as needed. In addition, the role supports enterprise applications and systems, including conducting testing and validation of system upgrades to ensure functionality and minimize disruption to operations.</div> 2621 - Registrar https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38346 2026-07-13T08:35:23-04:00 2026-07-13T08:35:24-04:00 IT Support Specialist <div>This position supports the UTS Active Directory project for the campus. The OU Tech Center will be responsible for all Device Lifecycle, Asset Management and Endpoint Device Management – quoting, imaging, configurations, setups, asset tagging, planning, implementing, and supporting the university’s endpoint management environment during and after the migration to the new Active Directory. This position ensures that all campus-owned computers and devices are securely configured, centrally managed using tools such as Jamf and InTune, and integrated with enterprise identity services such as Microsoft Entra. The role develops and maintains device management standards, deploys support and automation tools, and implements least-privilege access controls to protect institutional data while enabling efficient support for faculty, staff, and students.<br>Working collaboratively with infrastructure, security, and support teams, this position manages policies, configurations, and lifecycle processes for endpoints across campus. The role also supports the implementation of modern management practices, including device provisioning, patching, software deployment, and compliance monitoring. A key responsibility is ensuring that endpoint administration and support tools follow least-privilege principles and align with institutional security policies and regulatory requirements.Through effective governance, automation, and collaboration, the IT Support Specialists role will ensure a secure, scalable, and user-focused computing environment that supports the university’s academic, research, and administrative missions.</div> 0570 - UTS Help Desk and Desktop Services https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/37916 2026-05-29T16:06:27-04:00 2026-05-29T16:06:27-04:00 Electrification Lab Assistant 2185 - Electrical & Computer Engineering https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38967 2026-09-04T16:10:32-04:00 2026-09-04T16:10:33-04:00 Museum Technician <div>Under the supervision of the curator, this position cleans historical interior elements, rooms, and collections at Meadow Brook Estate, ensuring a safe, clean environment for Meadow Brook Hall's historical resources.<br><br></div><div>This position will carry out routine building and collections care duties according to schedules and seasonal needs. The person will identify the need for any non-routine building maintenance or repairs and consult with the Curator to determine appropriate procedures with regard to historic preservation guidelines and standards.<br><br></div><div>This position will support the Curator with handling collection objects, prepping for special displays and exhibits.<br><br>The person’s schedule will balance the needs of collections care, education, interpretation, and visitor safety and experience. The holder of this position will have a team approach and work well with staff, volunteers, and the public.</div> 3760 - Meadow Brook Estate https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/36043 2025-09-10T13:52:36-04:00 2025-09-10T13:52:36-04:00 Special Instructor - Counseling <div>The Department of Counseling at Oakland University, Rochester, Michigan is seeking applicants for a Special Instructor Faculty Position (Clinical Mental Health or School Counseling). The position is a full-time appointment with the possibility of summer teaching starting January 1, 2026. Special Instructor positions emphasize teaching and service activities. We will begin reviewing applications on October 1, 2025 and continue reviewing applications until the position is filled. The primary responsibilities of the position include:</div><div><br></div><div>Teach courses (4/4) at the masters and doctoral-levels:</div><div>● Teach across the CACREP curriculum including core and clinical courses</div><div>● Advise students</div><div>● Engage with curriculum planning and development</div><div><br></div><div>Service:</div><div>● Engage in service assignments at the Department, School, and University level</div><div>● Engage in program accreditation</div><div>● Engage in professional leadership within the counseling profession</div> 1770 - Counseling https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38866 2026-08-27T08:10:47-04:00 2026-08-27T08:10:47-04:00 Assistant Softball Coach <div>To assist the Head Softball Coach in administering all aspects of an educationally sound and competitive Division I women’s softball program.</div> 2836 - Athletics Administration"
    },
