vering clear, energetic, and professional in-game announcements that enhance the fan experience and support game operations across multiple sports. View Details Bookmark Athletics Facility Event Staff TC06433 2836 - Athletics Administration The Facility Event Staff position supports the successful operation of Oakland University Athletics facilities and game-day events. This casual role assists with event setup and breakdown, guest services, facility preparation, crowd management, and operational support to ensure a safe, welcoming, and professional environment for student-athletes, coaches, officials, fans, and guests.Facility Ev... View Details Bookmark Host/Hostess - VIP & Donor Rooms 06/10/2026 TC06431 2836 - Athletics Administration The Host/Hostess serves as the first point of contact for donors, sponsors, alumni, university leadership, and special guests attending Oakland University Athletics events. This position is responsible for creating a welcoming and professional atmosphere within VIP and donor hospitality areas while providing exceptional customer service and ensuring guests have an outstanding game-day experience. View Details Bookmark Athletics Ticket Staff 06/10/2026 TC06430 2836 - Athletics Administration To act as the front-line ambassador of our organization by managing point-of-sale transactions during sporting events. The role is designed to ensure guests receive a welcoming, efficient, and seamless experience when purchasing tickets. View Details Bookmark Athletics Broadcast Assistant 06/10/2026 TC06428 2836 - Athletics Administration To provide a specialized and technical skillset for our live sports productions. View Details Bookmark Accompanist 06/10/2026 TC06426 1203 - Music, Theatre & Dance The music department has a 19 hour (weekly) cap on casual staff (accompanist). Due to the influx of students in our program, our current staffing cannot meet the needs for our students are we require and additional accompanist to cover all assignments