    "https://jobs.oakland.edu/postings/38936": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Oakland University Employment Site | Accounting Office Part-Time Team Member Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Human Resources Benefits Campus Map Student Employment Accounting Office Part-Time Team Member Bookmark this Requisition Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Position Title Accounting Office Part-Time Team Member Department 2445 - Accounting Office Position Number X12445 Requisition No. TC06522 Salary Range/Pay Rate $45/hour Benefits of Working at Oakland University No benefits are associated with this position. Employee Group/Grade Temporary Job Category Casual /Temporary Casual/Temp Classification Work Schedule PT/Temp (20-39 hours, No Benefits ) Shift/Days Pay Schedule Hour Number of Hrs./Wk. Up to 39 hours per week Position Information Position Information Employee's Effective Start Date 09/14/2026 If this is a Temporary position, provide end date or enter N/A for any other position type. December 15, 2026 Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting or Finance. Strong knowledge of Microsoft Access and Excel or an equivalent combination of education and/or experience. A minimum of four years’ broad-based accounting experience. Ability to use financial accounting technology including computer-based spreadsheet and database applications. Ability to manage complex financial activities and projects. Excellent organizational and analytical skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to communicate effectively with others. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree. CPA designation. Higher education experience. Tax research and preparation experience. Position Purpose Position performs research and provides recommendations on various GASB and tax-related issues. Prepares financial analyses, assists with year-end closing, financial statement preparation and external audits. Performs various investment administration activities. Prepares various Federal, state and local tax returns. Works on various projects and other duties as assigned. Provides advice and training to other team members. Job Duties Position performs research and provides recommendations on various GASB and tax-related issues. Prepares financial analyses and schedules, assists with year-end closing, financial statement preparation and external audits. Performs various investment administration activities. Prepares various Federal, state and local tax returns. Works on various projects and other duties as assigned. Provides advice and training to other team members. Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No Position Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents 371 Wilson Boulevard, Rochester, MI 48309 248-370-2100     To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
